Minimal owned-choice research, 29 October 2026

The research question is whether the public finite pure fragment has
enough structure to justify a small calculus before adding hidden choices,
beliefs, control, or dependent types. This directory records an initial
theorem package. Originality is not established.

The intended signature retains internal role-switching. Start with
general.tex and symmetric.tex (PDFs in build/minimal after building).
The primary new structural results in general.tex are:

  - The entire idempotent full-signature clone is already generated by
    the K owned binary choices alone. A syntactic criterion recognizes it
    and extracts an equivalent term without constants or internal switches.
  - Every idempotent context therefore has the canonical K-player-view
    subdirect representation. Its ambiguous restriction is a nonempty join,
    giving a semilattice clone quotient and excluding near-unanimity and
    Mal'cev terms. Every occurring variable is essential; all core
    identities preserve their variable sets.
  - Optimal fixed idempotency domains have ceil(log2(K+1)) values at K>=4,
    and three at K=3. Explicit ambiguous domains attain these bounds.
  - Disjoint output requirements are jointly witnessed by one source
    occurrence. This holds at every arity, with internal permutations, and
    is kernel-checked in Separation.lean.
  - The deterministic atomic fragment is precisely the known clone S_2:
    essentially unary or at most two-valued functions. The upper bound
    applies the established Pol(iota_3)=S_2 theorem, cited explicitly.
    In particular idempotent atom-preserving contexts project one input.
  - Relative reset selects an atomic right operand, otherwise unions.
    Its homogeneous observation quotient is the standard right-normal-band
    clone. Mixed valuations refute associativity in the full algebra.
  - Unary ambiguity actions S -> S union sigma(S) have exact fibers given
    by cycle types, uniformly at K>=4. Long cycles impose coherence that
    refutes the proposed sufficiency of marginal atomic row bounds.
    All 282 four-role ambiguity actions without constant coordinates
    have this form up to an output permutation, with 6378 functions above.

general.tex identifies the ambiguity-action quotient at every K using an
affine extension of the known factorpower of the symmetric group. Its
canonical rows have an exact perfect-matching criterion and polynomial
recognition, synthesis, and composition. It also proves coNP-completeness
of equation validity, even at fixed K=3 without switches, and identifies
all unary units as role permutations at every K.
symmetric.tex proves optimal singleton/pair tests at every arity and the
exact three-role unary classification (751 functions). Its partial-
permutation quotient is precisely the K=3 specialization of general.tex.
structure.tex analyzes the no-switching reduct and the congruences of
both signatures. report.tex supplies the SPE interpretation, union
occurrence bound, and the reduct's unary classification.
The adjacent proposal-realization-and-sharing.md supplies the roadmap;
the union construction was already in that proposal.

From the repository root:

    make check-minimal
    make paper-minimal

The first command runs six Python experiments and kernel-checks
Basic.lean, Perspectives.lean, Synthesis.lean, and BooleanCore.lean using
Lean 4.34.1, plus Separation.lean for internal switches and reset. The
version is pinned by this directory's
lean-toolchain. Only Std is imported. Generated .olean files go to
build/minimal/lean. The second command builds all four notes.

Proof inventory:

    winners_node
        Exact SPE-winner recurrence, from full profiles and unrestricted
        whole-player deviations; SPE existence and local optimality.
    three_owner_join / neutralTree_winners
        Three distinct owners define neutral union.
    no_single_use_union
        Union cannot have just one occurrence of either input. The formal
        statement allows arbitrary nonempty side functions along a path.
        The syntax-to-path decomposition is explained in report.tex.
    uniform_copies_winners
        Fix any two component SPE profiles. Reusing identical full profiles
        in the copies achieves exactly their two winners. Deviations remain
        unrestricted; this is not an imperfect-information theorem.
    unary_normal_form_upper
        Every unary function is constant or has fixed extra winners on
        multiwinner inputs, with bounded rows on singleton inputs.
    ambiguity_unobservable_by_unique_winner
        Unique-winner tests identify all ambiguous sets under every unary
        context, even contexts containing multiple input occurrences.

    sameView_own / contextualAt_iff (Perspectives.lean)
        A player's exact contextual quotient: membership of that player,
        plus singleton tests for every other player. There are K+1 classes.
    small_counterexample / complete_test_domain
        At every arity, singletons plus ambiguous test sets omitting
        each player suffice. For a fixed observed player one prescribed
        pair is enough. The tests are input values, not a subalgebra.
    atom_collapse_to_top
        Identifying an atom with anything else forces its identification
        with the full winner set. This is the key extra constraint in the
        mathematical classification of every congruence.

    ground_realization / unary_synthesis (Synthesis.lean)
        Explicit terms realizing every nonempty constant and every reduct
        unary normal form. Only singleton leaves and owned choices occur.
    ambiguity_adder / singleton_separator / test_domain_necessary
        Constructed witnesses prove necessity of both conditions in the
        reduct's all-arity test-domain characterization.
    winners_instantiate / every_winner_set_realized
        Connect the synthesized terms to full-strategy SPE game semantics.

    boolean_gate / boolean_or / boolean_and (BooleanCore.lean)
        A definable gate onto {atom a, I} and the exact Boolean truth tables
        of two distinct owners on that carrier.
    Positive.compile_correct / Positive.equation_embedding
        Ordinary owned-choice terms encode every monotone Boolean formula;
        equation validity is preserved and reflected for all nonempty
        winner-set valuations. The SAT reduction and complexity-class
        claims are mathematical proofs in general.tex, not Lean statements.

    FullTerm.separation / FullTerm.input_separation (Separation.lean)
        One common syntactic source fits all disjoint target predicates.
        The syntax has winner constants, variables, owned choices, and
        explicit bijective internal role permutations.
    FullTerm.atomic_separation
        Injectively indexed singleton outputs arise from one variable
        occurrence and its accumulated permutation, jointly across tests.
    relativeReset_atom / relativeReset_multiple
        Exact generic semantics of relative reset over a list of owners.

Unary synthesis is now a generic Lean theorem. Uniqueness, counting, and
composition have mathematical proofs in report.tex and finite checks.
check.py independently exhausts the K=3 unary algebra (131
functions), constructs all normal forms for K=3,4 (131 and 6575), and checks
laws and uniform copies on finite models. Its fixed-profile SPE criterion
is separately justified by spe_node_iff in Lean.

The occurrence bound counts syntactic occurrences, not runtime duplication
or a required contraction rule. The observation is possible pure SPE
winners. It is neither forceability nor sequential equilibrium. Hidden
choices may destroy pure-equilibrium existence, so the public recurrence
must not be silently reused for them.

Both directions of the reduct's exact test-domain characterization are
now proved in Lean, using explicit syntactic witnesses for necessity.
Canonical status forms, the full congruence classification, the minimum
subdirect decomposition, and the internal-permutation congruence chain
have mathematical proofs in structure.tex, not complete Lean proofs yet.
check_structure.py verifies quotient operations for K=3..6; compares both
all-arity representations against full binary/ternary valuations; checks
all atom-containing test domains at K=3,4 against unary separation;
independently enumerates all congruences at K=3; constructs and checks the
626 classified congruences at K=4; and verifies the irreducible kernels
and symmetric congruence chains at both sizes.

The full signature makes one player's contextual quotient faithful to
the entire winner set; the K+1-state and K+2-test statements concern its
no-switching reduct. For the full signature, the optimal domain contains
every singleton and every pair. The full-signature provenance theorem,
pair-test theorem, and three-role unary classification currently have
mathematical proofs, not Lean proofs. check_symmetric.py independently
exhausts the 751 unary functions and synthesizes every normal form by an
actual term. It checks all 34^2 partial-permutation composition cases,
the sharp input separators for K=3..6, and binary/ternary provenance tests.

The general ambiguity monoid has written proofs in general.tex, not Lean
proofs yet. ambiguity.py implements its canonical rows, forced-edge
matching criterion, witness permutations, balanced term synthesis, and
composition. check_general.py independently exhausts the factorpowers
(49 and 7443 relations) and all admissible canonical rows (34 and 1979
actions) at K=3,4, and compares their affine quotients exactly. It checks
semantic uniqueness, every composition at K=3, 10000 compositions at K=4,
and synthesized terms. It also checks Boolean gates at K=3..6 and the
dual-rail SAT equivalence on 4369 small CNFs. These are complete checks
only at their stated finite sizes. General-K singleton fibers of the
unary monoid, a finite equational basis, and the residual bound remain
open. The monoid quotient is not claimed to classify full unary terms.

core.py recognizes idempotent terms and extracts their constant-free
owned syntax. check_core.py compares with full diagonal evaluation on
1200 terms at K=3..6, checks every ambiguous test domain at K=3,4, every
test domain against all unary operations at K=3, and constructs optimal
domains through K=64. The generic idempotent and test-domain theorems have
mathematical proofs, not Lean proofs yet.

fibers.py implements the relative-reset construction, exact cycle-fiber
synthesis, and synthesis of all deterministic atomic operations in S_2.
check_fibers.py compares the fiber formulas with independent closure under
all allowed permutation leaves, and checks actual terms on every winner
set. It covers every K=4 cycle type, longer cycles, and disjoint cycles.
It independently checks all 282 four-role supports without constant
coordinates, and all 19683 binary three-role tables against preservation
of iota_3; exactly 1545 pass, and every one is synthesized. The S_2
identification, its external clone-classification ingredient, the
right-normal-band observation quotient, and the generic cycle theorem
are not Lean proofs yet. General singleton fibers remain open.

An optional finite-basis experiment is available as:

    python3 research/minimal/probe_residual.py

It samples and certifies subdirectly irreducible quotients of a specified
79-element subalgebra of A_3^3. Its eight fixed trials find sizes 4 and 7.
This proves no bound on the generated variety and is not part of the
theorem checks. The verified Willard route still needs a residual bound.

External relabeling is a symmetry throughout. Prior art includes standard
Leibniz congruences, semilattice closure operators, and uniform matroids;
the specific classifications need a priority investigation.
